\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Schematic of the end states of newly formed throats, whatever their origin. A lone throat's perturbation sign selects collapse or inflation (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:branching}). A pair's relative charge sign selects repulsion or attraction (Sec.~\ref {sec:pair:sign}). The throats of a repelling pair inflate as it recedes (Sec.~\ref {sec:pair:recede}). An attracting pair merges if its common horizon forms early in the throats' inflation (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:race}); in a fast plunge it collapses to a merged core around which no common horizon is found (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:capture}). Gold: horizons; right: sketched wave signals. Two end states give a black hole after a single burst without a chirp, the fast plunge gives a merged core, and in every other end state the throats inflate.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fates}{{1}{3}{Schematic of the end states of newly formed throats, whatever their origin. A lone throat's perturbation sign selects collapse or inflation (Sec.~\ref {sec:single:branching}). A pair's relative charge sign selects repulsion or attraction (Sec.~\ref {sec:pair:sign}). The throats of a repelling pair inflate as it recedes (Sec.~\ref {sec:pair:recede}). An attracting pair merges if its common horizon forms early in the throats' inflation (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:race}); in a fast plunge it collapses to a merged core around which no common horizon is found (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:capture}). Gold: horizons; right: sketched wave signals. Two end states give a black hole after a single burst without a chirp, the fast plunge gives a merged core, and in every other end state the throats inflate}{figure.1}{}}
