\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Shape of the boosted throat at $t=0$: $\chi $ contours and their axis ratio against boost speed $v$. (a)~The $\chi $ contour just inside the throat, at rest and at $p=0.45$, the latter on its analytic ellipse; fainter ellipses continue the law to $v=0.7$ and $0.95$. (b)~Axis ratio (along/across the motion) against $v$, on the curve $1/\gamma =\sqrt  {1-v^2}$. (c)~Residual from $1/\gamma $ at three contour levels. The boosted data carry the special-relativistic shape, and both constraints hold at the discretisation error of the exact solution.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:boost_contraction}{{2}{5}{Shape of the boosted throat at $t=0$: $\chi $ contours and their axis ratio against boost speed $v$. (a)~The $\chi $ contour just inside the throat, at rest and at $p=\clmSpiralMomentumFlyby $, the latter on its analytic ellipse; fainter ellipses continue the law to $v=0.7$ and $0.95$. (b)~Axis ratio (along/across the motion) against $v$, on the curve $1/\gamma =\sqrt {1-v^2}$. (c)~Residual from $1/\gamma $ at three contour levels. The boosted data carry the special-relativistic shape, and both constraints hold at the discretisation error of the exact solution}{figure.2}{}}
