\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Minimal areal radius $R_{\min }$ of the isolated throat against time, from exact static data. (a)~Levels 2--4 without an added perturbation: level 3 (dashed), level 4 (solid) and level 2 (grey, failing first at the cross); dotted, $R_\star $. Dots mark where the radius scan loses the throat; muted lines continue its last reading. (b)~$|R-R_0|/R_0$ at levels 3 and 4, with small-amplitude exponential fits (gold). (c)~Level 3 with added perturbations, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light) and $\pm 0.1$ (heaviest); dashed, outward ($\varepsilon >0$); gold, local exponential fits; crosses, failures at the compactified origin. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(a,b). (d)~The Lorentz-boosted throat (dash-dot, $p=0.45$, level 3) against the resting level-3 run (grey). The throat leaves its static state on one exponential mode, the sign of the initial perturbation selects collapse or inflation, and uniform motion changes neither.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_throat}{{3}{8}{Minimal areal radius $R_{\min }$ of the isolated throat against time, from exact static data. (a)~Levels 2--4 without an added perturbation: level 3 (dashed), level 4 (solid) and level 2 (grey, failing first at the cross); dotted, $R_\star $. Dots mark where the radius scan loses the throat; muted lines continue its last reading. (b)~$|R-R_0|/R_0$ at levels 3 and 4, with small-amplitude exponential fits (gold). (c)~Level 3 with added perturbations, Eq.~\eqref {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light) and $\pm 0.1$ (heaviest); dashed, outward ($\varepsilon >0$); gold, local exponential fits; crosses, failures at the compactified origin. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(a,b). (d)~The Lorentz-boosted throat (dash-dot, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumFlyby $, level 3) against the resting level-3 run (grey). The throat leaves its static state on one exponential mode, the sign of the initial perturbation selects collapse or inflation, and uniform motion changes neither}{figure.3}{}}
