\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Separation changes of throats released from rest, for matched pairs (Sec.~\ref {sec:model:solve}): the sign rule (a,b), the force law (c) and its growth with throat width (d). (a)~Separation change of two $d=12$ pairs that differ only in the sign of one scalar: like-signed ($\sigma =+1$, dashed) and opposite-signed ($\sigma =-1$, solid). Separations are inverse-$\chi $-weighted centroids of the midplane $\chi $ minima, one per throat. (b)~Pull-to-push ratio against the prediction $(Q{+}1)/(Q{-}1)=3/2$ (gold), with $Q$ the scalar-to-gravity force ratio of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:force}. Excluded: the gauge-settling window $t<3.5$ (grey) and $t>10.5$ (open circles), where the closing pair has closed $4.6\%$ of its separation. (c)~Separation change by $t=11.5$ of like-signed pairs at $d=12/14/16/18$ (dots), against inverse-square in $d$ scaled through $d=12$ (grey, dashed) and $A/(d+\delta )^2$ fitted on $d=12$--$16$ (gold; dotted at $d=18$). (d)~The same at $d=12$ against throat width $a=1/1.5/2/3$, on logarithmic axes, with $a^2$ scaled through $a=2$ (grey, dashed) and a power-law fit (gold). Opposite-signed throats attract, and the like-signed push falls more slowly than inverse-square in $d$ and grows more slowly than $a^2$.}}{11}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pair}{{5}{11}{Separation changes of throats released from rest, for matched pairs (Sec.~\ref {sec:model:solve}): the sign rule (a,b), the force law (c) and its growth with throat width (d). (a)~Separation change of two $d=\clmPairSeparation $ pairs that differ only in the sign of one scalar: like-signed ($\sigma =+1$, dashed) and opposite-signed ($\sigma =-1$, solid). Separations are inverse-$\chi $-weighted centroids of the midplane $\chi $ minima, one per throat. (b)~Pull-to-push ratio against the prediction $(Q{+}1)/(Q{-}1)=\clmScalarQRatio $ (gold), with $Q$ the scalar-to-gravity force ratio of Eq.~\eqref {eq:force}. Excluded: the gauge-settling window $t<\clmSignSettleWindow $ (grey) and $t>\clmSignWindowEnd $ (open circles), where the closing pair has closed $\clmSignWindowClosed \%$ of its separation. (c)~Separation change by $t=11.5$ of like-signed pairs at $d=12/14/16/18$ (dots), against inverse-square in $d$ scaled through $d=12$ (grey, dashed) and $A/(d+\delta )^2$ fitted on $d=12$--$16$ (gold; dotted at $d=18$). (d)~The same at $d=12$ against throat width $a=1/1.5/2/3$, on logarithmic axes, with $a^2$ scaled through $a=2$ (grey, dashed) and a power-law fit (gold). Opposite-signed throats attract, and the like-signed push falls more slowly than inverse-square in $d$ and grows more slowly than $a^2$}{figure.5}{}}
