\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Areal radius and Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS of the head-on merger against time ($d=8$ from rest, opposite signs). The run has three restart segments (dashed rules at $t=35$ and $50.8$; levels named in each panel). Level 5 runs to a NaN in $h_{11}$ at the merged core at $t=38.845$, inside the MOTS (grey after it, up to the failure cross in (c)--(e)); level 6 restarts from the $t=35$ checkpoint; level 4 continues to $t=100$ with no NaN. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass. Gold: the MOTS finder (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}; post-processing MOTS search, one point per output slice), with the horizon forming at $t=18$ with $M_{\rm  MS}=2.817$ and regrowing by at most $0.34\%$; at $t=100$, $M_{\rm  MS}=2.3894$. Grey dashes: the round-sphere scan, late and small at formation and finding no surface over $t=26$--$35$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:contact}). Rules: one isolated throat, $R_\star =3.89$; $\sqrt  2R_\star $, a sphere with both throats' area; $2M_{\rm  ADM}$ ($M_{\rm  ADM}$ in (b)). (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ minima. (d)~$\max |K|$. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed). Gold dotted rule: horizon formation. Movie: Video~3; \href  {https://youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}}. The horizon shrinks toward the Schwarzschild radius of the pair's mass.}}{12}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headon_collapse}{{6}{12}{Areal radius and Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS of the head-on merger against time ($d=\clmHeadonSeparation $ from rest, opposite signs). The run has three restart segments (dashed rules at $t=\clmHeadonCsmSeamOne $ and $\clmHeadonCsmSeamTwo $; levels named in each panel). Level 5 runs to a NaN in $h_{11}$ at the merged core at $t=\clmHeadonCsmNanTime $, inside the MOTS (grey after it, up to the failure cross in (c)--(e)); level 6 restarts from the $t=35$ checkpoint; level 4 continues to $t=100$ with no NaN. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass. Gold: the MOTS finder (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}; post-processing MOTS search, one point per output slice), with the horizon forming at $t=\clmHeadonCsmMotsTime $ with $M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmMotsMass $ and regrowing by at most $\clmHeadonCsmRegrow \%$; at $t=100$, $M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmEndMass $. Grey dashes: the round-sphere scan, late and small at formation and finding no surface over $t=26$--$35$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:contact}). Rules: one isolated throat, $R_\star =\clmRstarShort $; $\sqrt 2R_\star $, a sphere with both throats' area; $2M_{\rm ADM}$ ($M_{\rm ADM}$ in (b)). (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ minima. (d)~$\max |K|$. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed). Gold dotted rule: horizon formation. Movie: Video~3; \href {https://youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/3sx9GHRTYVs}}. The horizon shrinks toward the Schwarzschild radius of the pair's mass}{figure.6}{}}
