\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Gravitational waveforms of every scenario against retarded time, one row per run. Left: $r\,\mathrm  {Re}\,\Psi _4$ of the dominant mode at the innermost sphere, each row on its own scale. Row (a) is the collapsing throat at $\varepsilon _2=0.05$, with the ringdown fit of Sec.~\ref {sec:single:gw} dashed. Caps mark where each drawn waveform ends: for the collapsing throat, before its numerical floor exceeds $14\%$ of the burst peak; for the fly-by and the plunge, where each run stops being reliable. Row (b) is the head-on run in the larger domain ($L=512$, spheres to $R=150$). The merger's waveform runs through the ringdown, interpolated linearly across one restart time. Grey under (b)--(d): the vacuum controls, black holes at the same $d$ and $p$, on the same scale. Right: the amplitude envelope at every sphere against its own retarded time (ink to faint, inner to outer), the upper envelope of $|r\Psi _4|$ for the complex $(2,2)$ modes and the analytic-signal envelope for the real $(2,0)$ modes. Gold dots mark the correlated wavefront (Sec.~\ref {sec:controls:bbh}). Movies of the head-on run in the larger domain and of the vacuum head-on and fly-by: Videos~11 \href  {https://youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}}, 8 \href  {https://youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}} and~9 \href  {https://youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}}. Every signal is outgoing and reaches the spheres in order of radius.}}{15}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_gallery}{{8}{15}{Gravitational waveforms of every scenario against retarded time, one row per run. Left: $r\,\mathrm {Re}\,\Psi _4$ of the dominant mode at the innermost sphere, each row on its own scale. Row (a) is the collapsing throat at $\varepsilon _2=\clmGwSeedStrong $, with the ringdown fit of Sec.~\ref {sec:single:gw} dashed. Caps mark where each drawn waveform ends: for the collapsing throat, before its numerical floor exceeds $\clmGwDrawFloorFrac \%$ of the burst peak; for the fly-by and the plunge, where each run stops being reliable. Row (b) is the head-on run in the larger domain ($L=\clmFarzoneBoxL $, spheres to $R=\clmFarzoneOuterR $). The merger's waveform runs through the ringdown, interpolated linearly across one restart time. Grey under (b)--(d): the vacuum controls, black holes at the same $d$ and $p$, on the same scale. Right: the amplitude envelope at every sphere against its own retarded time (ink to faint, inner to outer), the upper envelope of $|r\Psi _4|$ for the complex $(2,2)$ modes and the analytic-signal envelope for the real $(2,0)$ modes. Gold dots mark the correlated wavefront (Sec.~\ref {sec:controls:bbh}). Movies of the head-on run in the larger domain and of the vacuum head-on and fly-by: Videos~11 \href {https://youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/vesOxaP5GSg}}, 8 \href {https://youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/aRWvD4W8OOg}} and~9 \href {https://youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/65_3kw4obvE}}. Every signal is outgoing and reaches the spheres in order of radius}{figure.8}{}}
