\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Waveforms, spectra, frequencies and energies of every run, for a source of total mass $30\,M_\odot $ at $10$ Mpc, each in units of its own total mass. The vacuum control is two black holes with the separation and momentum of the $d=12$, $p=0.12$ run (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:capture}). (a)~Upper envelopes of $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere, aligned at each peak. (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities against the Advanced LIGO (aLIGO) design sensitivity (gold), each from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per waveform, ticked). The curves are falling power laws with no resolved maximum, so any apparent peak is the corner frequency $1/T$ of a waveform of duration $T$. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde  h|\propto f^{-7/6}$, up to its innermost stable circular orbit (ISCO) at $147$ Hz. (c)~Instantaneous frequency against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz); the vacuum control climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$, with $f$ the frequency and $M$ the total mass (Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole at the outermost sphere covering each waveform's window, the tick its change from the next sphere in; grey under each source, its vacuum control at the same $d$ and $p$. Open gold bars: published equal-mass vacuum values, all multipoles, for head-on infall from rest at infinity, $5.5\times 10^{-4}$~\cite  {witek2010}, and for quasi-circular inspiral and merger, $4.84\times 10^{-2}$~\cite  {scheel2009}. Each energy integrates $|\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ r\Psi _4\,\mathrm  {d}t'|^2$ over one retarded window, ending at the end of its reliable interval or where noise dominates, and is doubled for $\pm m$; gravitational channel only. Movie of the vacuum control: Video~10, \href  {https://youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}{\nolinkurl  {youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}}. Only the vacuum control climbs the chirp; no wormhole run does.}}{16}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_ligo}{{9}{16}{Waveforms, spectra, frequencies and energies of every run, for a source of total mass $\clmGwLigoMass \,M_\odot $ at $\clmGwLigoDist $ Mpc, each in units of its own total mass. The vacuum control is two black holes with the separation and momentum of the $d=12$, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumProd $ run (Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:capture}). (a)~Upper envelopes of $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere, aligned at each peak. (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities against the Advanced LIGO (aLIGO) design sensitivity (gold), each from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per waveform, ticked). The curves are falling power laws with no resolved maximum, so any apparent peak is the corner frequency $1/T$ of a waveform of duration $T$. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde h|\propto f^{-7/6}$, up to its innermost stable circular orbit (ISCO) at $\clmGwIscoHz $ Hz. (c)~Instantaneous frequency against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($\clmGwKerrHz $ Hz); the vacuum control climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=\clmGwTwinPeakFM $, with $f$ the frequency and $M$ the total mass (Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole at the outermost sphere covering each waveform's window, the tick its change from the next sphere in; grey under each source, its vacuum control at the same $d$ and $p$. Open gold bars: published equal-mass vacuum values, all multipoles, for head-on infall from rest at infinity, $\clmGwLitHeadonInfall $~\cite {witek2010}, and for quasi-circular inspiral and merger, $\clmGwLitCircular $~\cite {scheel2009}. Each energy integrates $|\int r\Psi _4\,\mathrm {d}t'|^2$ over one retarded window, ending at the end of its reliable interval or where noise dominates, and is doubled for $\pm m$; gravitational channel only. Movie of the vacuum control: Video~10, \href {https://youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}{\nolinkurl {youtu.be/NkcpGiJIxXI}}. Only the vacuum control climbs the chirp; no wormhole run does}{figure.9}{}}
