\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces (a)~Three-level factor $Q=(R_2-R_3)/(R_3-R_4)$ of the minimal areal radius against time for the static throat from exact data at levels 2--4; rules mark the orders $n=2$, 3, 4, and the dip at $t=16$ is one level-2 output time. (b)~$|r\Psi _4^{22}|$ at $R=20$ for the $d=12$, $p=0.12$ binary from Bowen--York initial data (not the boosted data used elsewhere) at throat level 5, its difference from level 4, and the change from refining the wave zone to half the base cell. (c)~Radiated energy on each sphere over that on the outermost sphere, against $R/M$, for the head-on run, the $d=6$ merger and the fly-by (ink) and two vacuum controls (grey). (d)~$|r\Psi _4^{20}|$ at $R=10$ for the head-on runs in the larger domain of Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}(b), at finest $\Delta x=1/16$, $1/32$ and $1/64$, and each neighbouring pair's difference (at most $0.55\%$, then $0.54\%$, of the peak); all three form the common MOTS at $t=18$. (e)~Shell averages of $\mathcal  {H}_{\rm  ADM}$ against $r$ outside the common MOTS (gold rule, its largest coordinate extent) for the same three runs at $t=100$, on the shared level-4 grid. The static throat converges at order $3.0$--$3.3$, the head-on energy at order $1.7$ and $\mathcal  {H}_{\rm  ADM}$ at order $1.7$, so the interior's constraint violation does not leak past the horizon.}}{19}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convergence}{{10}{19}{(a)~Three-level factor $Q=(R_2-R_3)/(R_3-R_4)$ of the minimal areal radius against time for the static throat from exact data at levels 2--4; rules mark the orders $n=2$, 3, 4, and the dip at $t=16$ is one level-2 output time. (b)~$|r\Psi _4^{22}|$ at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTwenty $ for the $d=12$, $p=\clmSpiralMomentumProd $ binary from Bowen--York initial data (not the boosted data used elsewhere) at throat level 5, its difference from level 4, and the change from refining the wave zone to half the base cell. (c)~Radiated energy on each sphere over that on the outermost sphere, against $R/M$, for the head-on run, the $d=6$ merger and the fly-by (ink) and two vacuum controls (grey). (d)~$|r\Psi _4^{20}|$ at $R=\clmExtractRadiusTen $ for the head-on runs in the larger domain of Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}(b), at finest $\Delta x=1/\clmConvFzDxLo $, $1/\clmConvFzDxMid $ and $1/\clmConvFzDxHi $, and each neighbouring pair's difference (at most $\clmConvFzPsiDiff \%$, then $\clmConvFzPsiDiffFine \%$, of the peak); all three form the common MOTS at $t=\clmConvFzMotsTime $. (e)~Shell averages of $\mathcal {H}_{\rm ADM}$ against $r$ outside the common MOTS (gold rule, its largest coordinate extent) for the same three runs at $t=100$, on the shared level-4 grid. The static throat converges at order $\clmConvOrderEvolLo $--$\clmConvOrderEvolHi $, the head-on energy at order $\clmConvFzOrder $ and $\mathcal {H}_{\rm ADM}$ at order $\clmConvFzHamOrder $, so the interior's constraint violation does not leak past the horizon}{figure.10}{}}
